{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-4115-r4517124","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Turkey Biscuit","sourcePageId":4115,"sourceRevision":"4517124","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-20T19:30:34Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Turkey%20Biscuit&oldid=4517124","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:27.026Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baked recipes","Category:Christmas recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for pot pie","Category:Recipes using cheddar","Category:Recipes using milk","Category:Recipes using turkey","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Thanksgiving recipes","Category:United States recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"064148e45b6a473e3f838368e5c01aa5e33e2f86bb3179f38e360fe64f02d2e7","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Turkey recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}| [[Cookbook:Meat and Poultry|Meat]]\n\nThis recipe is designed for using the leftover [[Cookbook:Turkey|turkey]] after a holiday meal, such as Thanksgiving or Christmas dinner.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n*4 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] cooked [[Cookbook:Turkey|turkey]] meat, [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*1 large [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], chopped\n*1 can cream of chicken soup\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Ranch Dressing|ranch dressing]]\n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n*¾ cup shredded [[Cookbook:Cheddar cheese|cheddar cheese]]\n*1 package frozen [[Cookbook:Biscuit|biscuit]] dough\n\n==Procedure==\n\n#[[Cookbook:Sautéing|Sauté]] the onion until tender.\n#Combine in a small bowl the all the other ingredients except the cheese and biscuits.\n#Stir this mixture, then place it into a [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|baking dish]], and [[Cookbook:Baking|bake]] for 15 minutes at 350°F until it is quite warm throughout.\n#Remove the baked mixture from the oven and sprinkle the shredded cheese on it. \n#Add a layer of frozen biscuits on top of this. Bake for about 20–30 minutes longer.\n#Serve.\n\n[[Category:United States recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pot pie]]\n[[Category:Recipes using turkey]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Christmas recipes]]\n[[Category:Thanksgiving recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cheddar]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Turkey Biscuit","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 cups cooked turkey meat, chopped","sourceText":"4 cups cooked turkey meat, chopped","amountText":"4 cups cooked turkey meat, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 large onion, chopped","sourceText":"1 large onion, chopped","amountText":"1 large onion, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 can cream of chicken soup","sourceText":"1 can cream of chicken soup","amountText":"1 can cream of chicken soup","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 tablespoons ranch dressing","sourceText":"2 tablespoons ranch dressing","amountText":"2 tablespoons ranch dressing","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ cup milk","sourceText":"½ cup milk","amountText":"½ cup milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"¾ cup shredded cheddar cheese","sourceText":"¾ cup shredded cheddar cheese","amountText":"¾ cup shredded cheddar cheese","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 package frozen biscuit dough","sourceText":"1 package frozen biscuit dough","amountText":"1 package frozen biscuit dough","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Sauté the onion until tender.","sourceText":"Sauté the onion until tender.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Combine in a small bowl the all the other ingredients except the cheese and biscuits.","sourceText":"Combine in a small bowl the all the other ingredients except the cheese and biscuits.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Stir this mixture, then place it into a baking dish, and bake for 15 minutes at 350°F until it is quite warm throughout.","sourceText":"Stir this mixture, then place it into a baking dish, and bake for 15 minutes at 350°F until it is quite warm throughout.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Remove the baked mixture from the oven and sprinkle the shredded cheese on it.","sourceText":"Remove the baked mixture from the oven and sprinkle the shredded cheese on it.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Add a layer of frozen biscuits on top of this. Bake for about 20–30 minutes longer.","sourceText":"Add a layer of frozen biscuits on top of this. Bake for about 20–30 minutes longer.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Serve.","sourceText":"Serve.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; pag